                    "a": "[[T]]Column A: Factors|Column B: Impacts on the development of Mauryan Empire;;Social|Mauryan society was based on seven classes — philosophers, farmers, soldiers, herdsmen, artisans, magistrates and administrators; city life grew and Taxila, Ujjain and Kashi were famous educational centres;;Political|Chandragupta Maurya established a central monarchy; his adviser Kautilya (Chanakya) wrote the Arthashastra, on whose principles the government was run; the empire was divided into four provinces and each province was administered by a royal prince;;Economic|Agriculture and trade were encouraged; trade routes became safe and cities grew; Pataliputra became a great trading city and silver coins were issued;;Administrative|Administration based on officials, the system of provinces and districts, law and order — all these kept the empire strong and organized[[/T]]",
