                    "a": "Hold up a pencil and ask whose it was? Obviously with only one clue, little can be said. Historians, generally, are much more helpless at that time, they are asked to make a judgement about a single object which someone must have lost. Much can be determined from the collection of lost objects, which are said to have been lost together.",
