                "items": [
                  {
                    "a": "Labour means pain and suffering.",
                    "q": "1. What is the literal meaning of labour?"
                  },
                  {
                    "a": "Labour means pain and suffering. It means a person manages his livelihood by working hard with his own hands and fulfills all his chores himself.",
                    "q": "2. Describe the concept of labour."
                  },
                  {
                    "a": "Personal benefits: Labour creates self-respect in man; it keeps a person active and saves him from illness and laziness; a hardworking man is saved from begging to someone. Social benefits: It brings progress and prosperity in society; hard work benefits not only the hard worker but also the country and the nation's progress.",
                    "q": "3. State the personal and social benefits of labour."
                  },
                  {
                    "a": "The Holy Qur'an says: 'Once the prayer is over, disperse throughout the land and seek the bounty of Allah. And remember Allah often so you may be successful'. (Al-Jumua: 10). The Holy Qur'an emphasizes earning by one's own hands. Prophets also earned a livelihood by their own hands. They never asked for wages to convey the message of Allah Almighty. The Holy Qur'an says: 'Say O Messenger! I ask no reward for it from you.' (Al-An'aam: 90)",
                    "q": "4. What does the Holy Qur'an teach about labour?"
                  },
                  {
                    "a": "The Holy Prophet highlighted the dignity of labour, saying: 'One who works hard is a friend of Allah'. On another occasion, the Holy Prophet stated: 'No one eats better food than that which he eats out of the work of his hands.' While teaching the value of hard work and the value of labour, he further said: 'Pay the labour his wages before his sweat dries.' The Holy Prophet disliked begging and said: 'The upper hand (i.e., helping hand) is better than the lower hand (i.e., begging hand)'.",
                    "q": "5. What is the teaching of the Holy Prophet about labour?"
                  }
                ],
